  */
 MEMORY
 {
-  FLASH : ORIGIN = 0x08002000, LENGTH = 120K
-  RAM   : ORIGIN = 0x20001028, LENGTH = 17720
+  FLASH : ORIGIN = 0x08002000, LENGTH = 1024K
+  RAM   : ORIGIN = 0x20001028, LENGTH = 20424
 }
+/* LENGTH was 17720 (end 0x20005560). The KD32F328's SRAM is 24 KB, to 0x20006000: sotto's
+ * ramprobe module wrote, read and held every word of 0x20005560-0x20005FFF on the radio
+ * (2026-11-07, docs/k6-modules.md), so the application has those 2720 bytes too. */
 
+/* 20440 less 16: 0x20005FF0-0x20005FFF is hal::txdog's note, kept across a reset. The stack starts
+ * below it. Neither the bootloader (its stack starts at 0x20004028 and grows down) nor Aura's
+ * startup touches it. The bootloader clears its own RAM, 0x20000000-0x20001027, at every reset:
+ * the note at 0x20000FF0 was lost there (2026-11-09). */
